# The build context is the repo root (compose and CI build with `context: .`), so this is the only
# .dockerignore Docker reads: one in frontend/ or backend/ would do nothing. Below, everything local or
# generated, wherever it sits, so the context stays small and never carries the family's config (data.json, exercises.json), the database, the legacy state, uploads or .env files.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/dev-dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
.env
.evidence
.playwright-mcp
backend/uploads
backend/test-*.json
backend/*.tmp
backend/*.invalid-*
tools/help-voice/out
tools/problem-gen/.out
docs

# Local or generated files git also ignores (a frontend/.env.local would be read by vite build)
**/.env*
**/*.local
tmp
.idea
.gemini
tools/help-voice/lines.json
tools/problem-gen/.sample.md
